          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In one sense of the term, a
            %em framing
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            is a choice of trivialization of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundle"} frame bundle
          %p
            A manifold that admits a framing is also called a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong parallelizable manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %strong parallelized manifold
          %p
            More generally, one means by a
            %em framing
            not a trivialization of the tangent bundle itself, but
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal bundle
                if the manifold is understood
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedded
                in some
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            %li
              %p
                of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+tangent+bundle"} stable tangent bundle
          %p
            Accordingly, a
            %em framed cobordism
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
            equipped with a framing on the underlying manifold (see also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MFr"} MFr
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dim
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim(X)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            of the manifold and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq dim(X)
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              \-framing
            to mean a trivialization of the “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-stabilized tangent bundle”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \oplus \mathbb{R}^{n-dim(X)}
            (where the right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct summand
            denotes the trivial real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n - dim(X)
            = succeed "-framed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+category"} cobordism category
            of framed
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            asserts essentially that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+cobordisms"} (∞,n)-category of cobordisms
            with
            = succeed "-framing" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+with+duals"} symmetric monoidal (∞,n)-category with duals
          %p
            Beware that there is also the term “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-framing"}> 2-framing
            ” due to (
            %a{:href => "#Atiyah"}> Atiyah
            ), which is related but different.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#lie_groups Lie groups
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              is a parallelizable manifold.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Every non-zero
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+vector+field"} invariant vector field
              on the Lie group provides an everywhere non-vanishing section of the tangent bundle.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (Stable homotopy elements)
            %p
              Left invariant framings
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}
              on compact connected Lie groups
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim(G)=k
              give rise to elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [G,\mathcal{L}]
              in the stable homotopy group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mi k
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_k^s
              of spheres. One can restrict attention to semisimple Lie groups
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              since this construction behaves well with respect to products,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to T\times G/T
              gives a framed diffeomorphism and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^1,\mathcal{L}] \in \pi_1^s
              is the generator. The following facts are assembled from (
              %a{:href => "#Ossa82"}> Ossa 1982
              ) and (
              %a{:href => "#Minami16"}> Minami 2016
              ).
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  For any
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+group"} semisimple
                  compact connected Lie group
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 72
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi G
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℒ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 72[G,\mathcal{L}]=0
              %li
                %p
                  The left invariant framings on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SO
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(n),Spin(n)
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(n)
                  give the zero element for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 7
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\geq 7
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(n)
                  for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 4
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\geq 4
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mn 4
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 6
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 7
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 8
                          %mo ,
                          %mi SO
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 4
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi SO
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 6
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 5
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 6
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_4,E_6,E_7,E_8, SO(4),SO(6),SU(5),SU(6)
              %li
                %p
                  The left invariant framings on the remaining groups (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi Sp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
